"""
CES Oracle -> SQL Server refresh driver.

- Iterates every table in one run.
- INSERT order (parents first) comes from ces_refresh_config.json -> settings.tables.
- DELETE order (children first) is the reverse of that list.
- FULL mode = reverse-order DELETE for all tables, then forward-order INSERT.
  This satisfies FK constraints across the whole schema.
- Identity columns are preserved via SET IDENTITY_INSERT ON.

Run:
    python ces_refresh_all.py

Modes (env CES_REFRESH_MODE, overrides config default):
    FULL   - delete everything, then insert everything (default)
    INSERT - insert only (no delete)
    DELETE - delete only
"""
